 "about_text": "Nazarian / Curcio is a contemporary art gallery in Los Angeles, owned by Shulamit Nazarian and Seth Curcio. Nazarian founded the gallery in Venice, CA in 2012, initially focusing on artists from the greater Middle East. Curcio joined in 2016, and together they broadened the program to emerging, mid-career, and established artists whose work engages social and political issues through personal narrative. In 2017 the gallery moved to a 6,000-square-foot, two-story building on La Brea Avenue in Hollywood, with two exhibition spaces, a library, offices, and viewing rooms. The gallery represents artists based in the U.S. and abroad, with an emphasis on those working in Los Angeles, and regularly participates in major national and international art fairs.",
